            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What warranty does Tru Grit give?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Dealers list a lifetime frame warranty on the Grit Runner, with two years on the resistance belt, tread and monitor. For the Elite, dealers disagree: one lists lifetime frame and belt with 5 years on the tread and 3 on the monitor. Ask your dealer who handles claims.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is the Tru Grit Runner on Amazon?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Yes. An Amazon listing titled Tru Grit Fitness Runner Curved Manual, with six resistance levels and an LCD, matched the standard Grit Runner on 4 November 2026. We did not find an Amazon listing for the Elite. Check the seller and warranty before buying.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is the Tru Grit Runner good for HYROX training?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                It is one of the cheapest curved treadmills with settings designed for sled pushes, which makes it a budget option for HYROX-style running and push work. The official HYROX race treadmill, the Centr x HYROX Perform Tread, has eight magnetic levels and costs $6,999.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div class="mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes Buying a Tru Grit Treadmill</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The Grit Runner’s price is its attraction. These are the ways buyers end up regretting it.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying from the first dealer you find</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The same Grit Runner was listed from $1,996 to $3,299 on one day. Compare at least three dealers, and include the freight charge and returns terms in the comparison.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Not asking who handles the warranty</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">With Tru Grit’s own website unreachable when we checked, the dealer is your route to a claim. Choose one that says in writing that it handles warranty service, and ask whether it stocks slats and monitors.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying the Elite without a weight rating</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Tru Grit does not publish the Elite’s maximum user weight. At $3,495 you can buy an AssaultRunner Pro rated for 350 lb or a TrueForm Trainer rated for 400 lb. Get the Elite’s figure in writing before ordering if you are heavy.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Expecting a refined running feel</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Independent reviews criticise the standard Runner’s slat gaps, finish and noise at a sprint. It is a conditioning tool at a low price. If smooth daily running matters most, spend more or look at the SOLE C80.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

