        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Tru Grit makes two curved manual treadmills: the Grit Runner, $1,996 to
          $3,299 at dealers, and the Grit Runner Elite at $3,495.</strong> The standard Runner is one of the
          cheapest curved treadmills with real sled-push settings and a 330 lb rating, and a reasonable buy from
          a dealer that will handle warranty claims, given that Tru Grit's own website was not working when we
          checked.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The Elite is harder to recommend: at the same price the
          <a href="/assaultrunner-pro-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">AssaultRunner Pro</a>
          and <a href="/trueform-treadmills/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">TrueForm Trainer</a>
